# Unified, with the default three lines of context.
#
# `tworoutes:` -- and the reason is the header rather than the diff. A unified
# header carries each file's modification time, and standard input has none, so
# both this program and the tool stamp a pipe with the moment they ran. The
# file route is what is held against the oracle; the pipe route cannot be held
# against the file route because the two are not describing the same thing.
args: -u
tworoutes:
first:
alpha
bravo
charlie
delta
echo
foxtrot
input:
alpha
bravo
CHARLIE
delta
echo
foxtrot
